## 1. Proposed workspace

### Folder tree and addresses

```text
D:\Git\lib-build\                       git worktree of Amalgamour/Librarian, branch workshop
├─ README.md                            door for people
├─ AGENTS.md                            the one boot file (CLAUDE.md and GROK.md are pointers carrying the same block)
├─ .gitignore                           .librarian/  __pycache__/  out/
├─ 00.kernel\                           desk 00, owner address 00.00.00.kernel
│  ├─ 00.md 00.start.md 00.about.md 00.readme.md 00.live     desk files (law 0051); 00.live written by compute only
│  ├─ 00.00.00.syntax\                  book: syntax
│  ├─ 00.00.01.law\                     book: law (role definitions land here, draft)
│  └─ 00.00.10.work\                    book: work (decision D1)
│     ├─ 00.md 0010.about 0011.contents 0014.design 0056.band
│     ├─ 0100.band.returns   01NN       builder returns
│     ├─ 0200.band.code      02NN       code being written
│     ├─ 0300.band.compute   03NN       running modules: 0302.run 0303.jobs 0304.check 0305.clerk 0306.slot 0307.face
│     ├─ 0400.band.dev       04NN       designs, Director decisions, goal, seat assignments
│     ├─ 0500.band.packs     05NN       packs
│     └─ 0600.band.notes     06NN       findings, carried threads
├─ app\                                 app shell, "at the top, alongside the desk" (1008 05.01 #01)
│  ├─ librarian.py                      the one supported entry
│  └─ tests\                            integration and acceptance tests
└─ .librarian\                          app state, journal, last-visit; outside git (1008 05.01 #12)
```

**Why the desk is `00`.** The Director wants one desk holding syntax, law and work. Kernel law makes a desk's own books the shelf-00 books (`DD.00.BB`, in `00.00.00.kernel.draft/00.md`). At desk 10, syntax and law would be local overrides of a kernel living somewhere else, which means two desks. Desk 00 also keeps every existing reference to `00.00.00` and `00.00.01` valid.

**Why the work book is `10`.** Law `0054.book` says a book takes "the first open slot from 10 up". But law `0018.seqaddr` (Walk) says "Desk books are 00 and 01", and Grok's draft `00.kernel/00.md` says "No real work is placed here". So the address needs the Director's ruling (D1).

### Code, ownership and the entry

**Where code lives.**
- A module's code sits physically on its compute page, as `02.name.py`. This is the Director's decision from `rebuild/00.md`, Faces, and `0300.band.compute/05.01`.
- The page number is the owning lane (one number, one name).
- `app/` holds no module logic. It has the entry shim and the integration tests.

**Tests.**
- A module's self-test stays inside it, as `<module> test`, following the existing convention.
- Tests that cross modules go in `app/tests`.

**Generated output.** `.librarian/`, `__pycache__/` and `out/`, none of them committed.

**The one supported entry.** `python app/librarian.py <module> <command> [args]`, for example `python app/librarian.py jobs find 0401.goal`.
1. It walks up from the current folder to `00.kernel/00.md`.
2. It runs the loader at `00.00.10.work/0302.run/02.run.py`.

The loader is imported to `0302` as a draft. Importing isn't seating, and this also removes the `0202`/`0302` mismatch that Codex found (`1001.assessment` F04).

### Branch, checkout and starting commit

**Setup.** `git worktree add D:\Git\lib-build -b workshop 14676ca`, starting from `origin/main`.

**What that commit brings:**
- The full tree as recorded in `1ea63a8`: both kernels, `10.workshop` as of then, zips, `Research`, `colab`.
- `README.md` (`38a037e`).
- Grok's handoff report.
- History shared with `rebuild`. That lets imports come straight from commits (`git show de3b8eb:<path>`), and makes the later merge into `main` an ordinary merge.

**First commit on `workshop`: clear the floor.** Remove the inherited tree from this branch only. It stays in `main`'s history, on `rebuild`, and under the archive tags. Then import selectively.

**Why not an orphan branch.** It would make the later merge into `main` an unrelated-history merge.

